ISO-10303-21;
/* Twi165: Single ADVANCED_FACE on PLANE in CLOSED_SHELL; outer EDGE_LOOP has 4 edges: E0 LINE (0,0,0)→(10,0,0) — lead-in straight edge; E1 degree-3 B-spline (10,0,0)→(14,3,0) sub-curve #1 with C1 kink at start; E2 degree-3 B-spline (14,3,0)→(12,7,0) sub-curve #2 with C1 kink at junction; E3 degree-3 B-spline (12,7,0)→(0,0,0) sub-curve #3 with C1 kink at junction; E1/E2/E3 represent subdivided single logical curve; C1 tangent-discontinuity at every sub-curve boundary IS the defect; CheckTail without knot-continuity awareness fires at each junction as tail failure over-reporting defects IS the mechanism; EDGE_LOOP IS wired into FACE_OUTER_BOUND → ADVANCED_FACE in CLOSED_SHELL — never orphaned */
